## Uninstall

{# Printed with the real token for the person whose trial it is, so the line runs as it stands even
   on a machine that never installed it — settling the trial needs the token, not the local record. #}
```bash
{% if ctx.trial %}
autoskill trial remove {{ ctx.trial_session_id or "<trial-id>" }}{% if ctx.trial_token %} --token {{ ctx.trial_token }}{% endif +%}
{% else %}
autoskill remove {{ ctx.skill_name }} --target {{ adapter.id }}
{% endif %}
```

{% if ctx.trial %}
This removes the trial copy and tells AutoSkill the outcome. To keep it instead, replace `remove` with
`accept` — that swaps the trial copy for the final version, which runs without checkpoints.
{% else %}
This deletes the skill folder, unregisters the MCP servers it added and removes the private
environments installed with it. Anything that was there before the install is put back.
{% endif %}

